# AC semantic probe: persisted cache roundtrip (PLAN-796 T-06, executed)

status: executed — cold publish, REAL worker process restart (the
`restart` step ends the session; the next query runs in a FRESH worker
process against the same store root), then a body edit flips the key.
The no-compute-on-hit control is a declarable oracle
(compute_calls: 0).

```test-case
case {
  schema: "autolang.case/2"
  id: "ac.sema.cache-roundtrip"
  tags: ["ac-semantics", "probe"]
  source: { file: "src/cache-roundtrip.at", syntax: "auto", path: "cache-roundtrip.at" }
  entry: { mode: "program" }
  checks: [
    { id: "roundtrip", adapter: "probe", action: "run",
      options: {
        recipe: "sema/query-v1",
        sema: { package: "probe", module: "cache-roundtrip", kind: "infer-body", fn: "main" },
        steps: [
          { op: "query" },
          { op: "restart" },
          { op: "query" },
          { op: "edit-source", from: "x * 2", to: "x * 3" },
          { op: "query" }
        ]
      },
      expect: { completion: "success", probe: [
        { cache: "published", compute_calls: 1,
          stages_include: ["infer", "publish"],
          bindings_file: "oracle/ac.sema.cache-roundtrip.bindings.json" },
        { cache: "hit", compute_calls: 0 },
        { cache: "published", compute_calls: 1 }
      ] } }
  ]
}
```
